<h1>Grooveli AI Research & Model Evaluation Report: Addendum & Product Integration Extension</h1>
<div class="subtitle">
  <strong>Document Type:</strong> Official Addendum & Extension &nbsp;|&nbsp; 
  <strong>Base Reference:</strong> Grooveli AI Research Model Evaluation Report (v1.0) &nbsp;|&nbsp; 
  <strong>Date:</strong> September 9, 2026
</div>

<hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #E2E8F0; margin: 16px 0;">

<h2>1. Purpose of this Addendum</h2>
<p>This document serves as an <strong>official extension and addendum</strong> to the initial <em>Grooveli AI Research & Model Evaluation Report (v1.0)</em>. While the primary research report successfully established a 10-step methodology, provider adapter principles, and initial candidate lists for TTS, ASR, and Lyria 3 music generation, this addendum expands the scope to cover all <strong>6 Grooveli AI Studio Product Modules</strong>.</p>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Key Objective:</strong> Complement the base 10-step evaluation framework by mapping model candidates, latency SLAs, unit margins, circuit breaker failovers, and billing safeguards for the full 6-module AI Studio suite.
</div>

<h2>2. Complete 6-Module Model Matrix</h2>
<p>The initial report focused on TTS, ASR, LLMs, and Music Synthesis. The table below extends that research to include the remaining missing audio DSP modules (<strong>Vocal Stem Separation</strong> and <strong>AI Audio Mastering</strong>).</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 22%;">AI Studio Module</th>
      <th style="width: 23%;">Primary Candidate Engine</th>
      <th style="width: 23%;">Secondary / Fallback Engine</th>
      <th style="width: 17%;">Delivery Mode</th>
      <th style="width: 15%;">Target Speed</th>
      <th style="width: 15%;">Target Margin</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>1. Lyric Assistant</strong></td>
      <td>Claude 3.5 Sonnet (Anthropic)</td>
      <td>GPT-4o (OpenAI) / Llama 3.3</td>
      <td>Real-Time Text Stream</td>
      <td>&lt; 0.35 seconds</td>
      <td class="badge-green">82% Margin</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>2. Voice Clone Studio</strong></td>
      <td>Fish Audio S2.1 Pro / Qwen3-TTS</td>
      <td>CosyVoice 3.5 / F5-TTS</td>
      <td>Real-Time Audio Stream</td>
      <td>&lt; 0.45 seconds</td>
      <td class="badge-green">70% Margin</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>3. Beat & Track Generator</strong></td>
      <td>Google Lyria 3 Pro API</td>
      <td>Stability Audio 2.0 / AudioCraft</td>
      <td>Chunked Audio Stream</td>
      <td>&lt; 1.20 seconds</td>
      <td class="badge-green">65% Margin</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>4. Stem Separator</strong> <em>(New)</em></td>
      <td>Hybrid Spectrogram Demucs v4</td>
      <td>HTDemucs Serverless Engine</td>
      <td>Background Async Job</td>
      <td>&lt; 12 seconds</td>
      <td class="badge-green">78% Margin</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>5. AI Mastering Studio</strong> <em>(New)</em></td>
      <td>Matchering 2.0 + Librosa DSP</td>
      <td>Matchering Cloud Worker</td>
      <td>Background Async Job</td>
      <td>&lt; 15 seconds</td>
      <td class="badge-green">85% Margin</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>6. Co-Writer Copilot</strong></td>
      <td>GPT-4o Interactive Model</td>
      <td>Claude 3.5 Haiku</td>
      <td>Bi-Directional WebSocket</td>
      <td>&lt; 0.25 seconds</td>
      <td class="badge-green">80% Margin</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>3. Automated Circuit Breaker & Failover Specification</h2>
<p>To enforce the 99.9% availability requirement outlined in the base report, all provider adapters will operate under an automated 4-step Circuit Breaker failover rule:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 15%;">Step</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">State / Trigger</th>
      <th style="width: 35%;">System Behavior</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">User Experience</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Step 1</strong></td>
      <td>Normal Operation</td>
      <td>Requests route to the Primary AI Engine (e.g., Fish Audio for Voice Cloning).</td>
      <td>Instant audio playback (&lt; 0.45s).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Step 2</strong></td>
      <td>Outage Detection</td>
      <td>System detects 3 consecutive errors or response delays exceeding 1.5 seconds.</td>
      <td>No error shown to user.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Step 3</strong></td>
      <td>Automatic Switch</td>
      <td>Circuit Breaker trips to "Open" and instantly routes request to Secondary Engine (e.g., Qwen3-TTS).</td>
      <td>Uninterrupted audio generation.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Step 4</strong></td>
      <td>Recovery & Reset</td>
      <td>System tests Primary Engine after 60 seconds; automatically restores primary routing once healthy.</td>
      <td>Continuous 99.9% service availability.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>4. Financial Unit Economics & Profit Safeguards</h2>
<p>Extending the credit engine concept from Section 8 of the base report, credit pricing is bound to API costs via the formula below:</p>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>Pricing Formula:</strong> Credit Retail Price = Wholesale API Cost / (1 - Target Gross Margin Percentage)
</div>

<table>
